# ~/.zshrc.local.example
# Template for machine-specific zsh configuration
#
# Copy this file to ~/.zshrc.local and customize for your machine
# This file is sourced at the end of .zshrc and is NOT tracked in git
#
# Use this for:
# - Machine-specific paths
# - API keys and tokens
# - Work-specific configurations
# - Experimental aliases/functions
# - Any settings you don't want in version control

# Example: Custom PATH additions
# export PATH="$HOME/custom/bin:$PATH"

# Example: API keys - read them from the macOS Keychain instead of storing them in plain text.
# Store once (prompts for the value, so it doesn't end up in shell history):
#   security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s openai-api-key -w
# Then:
# export OPENAI_API_KEY="$(security find-generic-password -a "$USER" -s openai-api-key -w 2>/dev/null)"
#
# For GitHub, prefer `gh auth login` (stores the token in the Keychain) over GITHUB_TOKEN.
